WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:11.810
Come on, let's go! Let's move forward together towards final victory!

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.200
A new atomic bomb, every 6 weeks.

00:00:35.852 --> 00:00:41.288
Gone are the days when our enemies could threaten us with nuclear weapons.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:52.260
Saying I've got the H-bomb means I now have the capacity to wreak mass

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:55.050
destruction on an opposing country.

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:06.565
There's only one person in the world today who's more unpredictable than Kim

00:01:06.565 --> 00:01:08.899
Jong-un, and that's Donald Trump.

00:01:11.997 --> 00:01:18.194
North Korea had better stop making threats against the United States,

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:22.949
or face fire and fury.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:30.134
As a child, I thought Americans were wolves, animals that take on the appearance

00:01:30.134 --> 00:01:31.137
of human beings.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:39.500
Kim Jong-un is the spitting image of his grandfather.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:44.900
He's strong-willed, determined and has a big ego.

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:04.846
The Italian Mafia has never reached the level of sophistication,

00:02:04.846 --> 00:02:10.340
size and global reach of North Korean organized crime.

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:19.670
We don't know what to do with North Korea, we've tried everything.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:25.430
The moment of truth is approaching.

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:59.010
We are in Vienna, at the United Nations nuclear monitoring center.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:03.880
That night, the experts are awakened by a seismic alert.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:18.870
Our monitoring system has been put on alert by a seismic event on the Korean peninsula.

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:29.066
We have automatic processing that tells us immediately whether it's an

00:03:29.066 --> 00:03:32.492
earthquake or whether there's a possibility of an explosion.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:43.428
We know immediately, from the shape of the signal, that it's not an earthquake

00:03:43.428 --> 00:03:44.731
but a nuclear test.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:48.680
The coordinates point to this mountainous area in North Korea.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:57.190
The country has already tested 5 atomic bombs on this site over the last ten years.

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:05.348
It's the only country still conducting nuclear tests, since all the others have

00:04:05.348 --> 00:04:07.049
stopped 20 years ago.

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:12.110
And North Korea makes no secret of the fact.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:14.270
Quite the contrary, in fact.

00:04:14.465 --> 00:04:18.550
A few hours after the explosion, state television interrupted its programs for

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:19.859
an official announcement.

00:04:20.087 --> 00:04:23.246
North Korea's nuclear engineers have successfully tested an H-bomb for

00:04:23.246 --> 00:04:25.187
intercontinental missiles at our test site,

00:04:25.283 --> 00:04:29.207
an H-bomb designed for intercontinental missiles.

00:04:29.303 --> 00:04:33.676
This is in line with the Workers' Party of Korea's plan to build a strategic

00:04:33.676 --> 00:04:34.482
nuclear force.

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:38.400
North Korean leader Kim Jong-un is delighted.

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:45.250
He has just tested an H-bomb, 16 times more powerful than the Hiroshima bomb.

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:48.720
To say "I've got the H-bomb",

00:04:48.828 --> 00:04:56.784
means I now have the capacity to inflict mass destruction on an opposing country.

00:04:58.522 --> 00:05:02.599
The second thing is to say that I have the capacity to do something that

00:05:02.649 --> 00:05:06.291
that, until now, only the big countries have been able to do.

00:05:09.486 --> 00:05:11.769
This is very advanced technology.

00:05:12.502 --> 00:05:14.498
If you have it, you're in the Club.

00:05:14.548 --> 00:05:16.770
If you don't, you're despised.

00:05:18.462 --> 00:05:22.040
Kim Jong-un is now awaiting reactions from the international community.

00:05:24.906 --> 00:05:31.659
North Korea's nuclear test seriously violated international rules. China is

00:05:31.659 --> 00:05:33.549
firmly opposed to it.

00:05:36.536 --> 00:05:41.169
We will be discussing the strengthening of European sanctions against North

00:05:41.169 --> 00:05:43.331
Korea. This is a matter of urgency.

00:05:46.464 --> 00:05:51.629
Military action is certainly an option. Is it inevitable? Nothing is inevitable.

00:05:51.679 --> 00:05:56.070
I hope we won't have to resort to military action against North Korea.

00:05:56.312 --> 00:06:00.799
That would be a very sad day for North Korea.

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:05.630
The North Korean leader is on the radar of the great powers.

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:08.136
And that's what he was hoping for.

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:12.160
To be taken seriously, particularly by the United States.

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:18.660
What the North Koreans want is for the United States to feel threatened.

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:24.021
And they're going the extra mile, giving the outside world - and especially the

00:06:24.021 --> 00:06:25.723
Americans - the impression that they're crazy,

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:27.320
that they're crazy.

00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:55.200
At 33, Kim Jong-un is the unbridled leader of North Korea's totalitarian regime.

00:06:56.230 --> 00:07:00.350
A few months earlier, he was commemorating the 105th birthday of his grandfather,

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:04.710
the late Kim Il-sung, founder of the regime in 1948.

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:09.870
It was he who launched North Korea into the nuclear race in the 1960s.

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:28.120
So it's his grandson who is at the heart of all concerns.

00:07:32.681 --> 00:07:35.360
One wonders if he really has a good head on his shoulders.

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:40.360
He's very emotional, even angry.

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:48.260
He sometimes puts his ego before reason.

00:07:50.510 --> 00:07:55.170
That's why he's perhaps more dangerous than his father or grandfather.

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:02.020
Kim Jong-un is uncontrollable.

00:08:02.820 --> 00:08:05.040
He wants to show the world his power.

00:08:06.220 --> 00:08:08.362
That's a risk for every country.

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:21.170
Kim Jong-un likes to stage these threats.

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:27.847
The day after the military parade, he organizes a grand spectacle in praise of

00:08:27.847 --> 00:08:28.497
the army.

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:37.710
This was Nixon's strategy.

00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:41.730
If the Russians thought the Americans were crazy, they'd be more careful.

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:44.910
That's what the North Koreans are doing, only much more muscular.

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:52.093
The North Korean leader even went so far as to reproduce in computer-generated

00:08:52.093 --> 00:08:56.252
images the explosion of a nuclear missile on an American city.

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:06.570
The message has never been so explicit, and no one knows how seriously to take it.

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:14.700
North Korea is a huge black hole for American intelligence.

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:20.780
The regime's decisions are often indecipherable.

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:30.372
The absence of real-time information on the North Korean leader's strategic

00:09:30.372 --> 00:09:33.123
intentions is a huge problem for us.

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:37.520
It's a situation that no American president has ever had to face before.

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:53.014
Faced with Kim Jong-un's nuclear provocations, the international community seems paralyzed.

00:09:53.081 --> 00:09:56.445
But how could such a small country, cut off from the rest of the world, acquire

00:09:56.445 --> 00:09:57.127
nuclear weapons?

00:09:57.220 --> 00:10:01.553
To understand this, we need to go back 70 years, to the time when the North

00:10:01.553 --> 00:10:03.402
Korean dictatorship was founded.

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:06.640
As you will see, Kim Jong-un is merely the heir to a system.

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:11.150
It all began in 1948, during the Second World War. Americans and Soviets

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:13.063
liberated Korea from the Japanese.

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:15.840
They now wanted to share the running of the country.

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:19.368
The South for the Americans and the North for the Soviets.

00:10:19.807 --> 00:10:24.850
With an arbitrary border dividing the peninsula in two, the 38th parallel.

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:29.620
In North Korea, Stalin was looking for a leader who could defend Soviet interests.

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:32.460
And he thought he had found the ideal candidate.

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:34.420
A certain Kim Il-sung.

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:43.025
In September 1948, the first legislative elections were held in the new People's

00:10:43.025 --> 00:10:44.327
Republic of Korea.

00:10:46.670 --> 00:10:48.890
On that day, a man came to power.

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:56.040
The new Prime Minister, a certain Kim Il-sung. He was barely 36.

00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:00.320
A very young man.

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:05.480
A big surprise in a still very traditional country where age is everything.

00:11:05.900 --> 00:11:07.629
Many wondered.

00:11:07.824 --> 00:11:11.320
Is it really possible to have such a young leader?

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:21.200
The country's other communist leaders don't really respect him.

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:24.340
Because he lacked diplomatic and political experience.

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:31.590
Yet it was he who Stalin sought to install in power in North Korea.

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:37.270
For he had long proved his bravery and loyalty to Soviet power.

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:49.540
He had been part of a Soviet military unit for several years on Russian soil.

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:51.980
His children had been born in the USSR.

00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:56.280
The Russians knew him well and trusted him.

00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:02.020
Stalin preferred someone young who could be manipulated.

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:06.829
He was convinced that he would be able to manipulate Kim Il-sung perfectly and

00:12:06.829 --> 00:12:11.639
that, all in all, he would be a sort of Soviet Union sub-prefect in North Korea.

00:12:12.420 --> 00:12:14.207
But Stalin was wrong.

00:12:14.470 --> 00:12:16.890
Kim Il-sung was not the puppet he thought he had put in power.

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:20.110
On the contrary, he was a man of great ambition.

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:28.368
With the Russians, Kim Il-sung is very subtle, very respectful. He's the perfect

00:12:28.368 --> 00:12:32.712
pupil and he plays, I'd say, low profile for two or three years.

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:36.867
But he wants power, he wants absolute power where he is and he wants power

00:12:36.867 --> 00:12:40.488
throughout the peninsula to establish his domination once and for all.

00:12:42.040 --> 00:12:46.140
Kim Il-sung has a secret dream: to reign over a reunified Korea.

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:50.150
But for this, he needs Soviet support.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:04.810
In March 1950, Kim Il-sung made an official visit to Moscow.

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:09.160
Stalin invited him to dine face-to-face in his dacha.

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:17.430
Kim Il-sung took advantage of the occasion to reveal his plans.

00:13:18.990 --> 00:13:23.690
His dream is to destabilize the South so that the regime collapses.

00:13:23.970 --> 00:13:28.677
So the only solution is war, i.e. to invade the South, which he is convinced

00:13:28.677 --> 00:13:30.908
will collapse like a house of cards.

00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:38.350
What Kim Il-sung wants is logistical help, buying weapons if necessary,

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:41.604
financial support too, and then political backing.

00:13:42.390 --> 00:13:46.030
The Korean leader was convincing, but Stalin hesitated.

00:13:46.226 --> 00:13:50.390
Attacking South Korea also meant attacking the United States.

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:53.870
In the midst of the Cold War, this was taking far too many risks.

00:13:55.300 --> 00:14:00.023
What Stalin wanted to be sure of was that there would be no strategic, i.e.

00:14:00.023 --> 00:14:03.677
nuclear, shift. Basically, why not have a traditional war?

00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:08.732
It should not degenerate into block-to-block confrontations with atomic weapons.

00:14:08.732 --> 00:14:10.417
That's what's not possible.

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:15.020
Stalin remained cautious. He agreed to help Kim Il-sung conquer the South,

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:21.445
but he would only supply equipment. No Soviet soldiers would reinforce the North

00:14:21.445 --> 00:14:22.485
Korean troops.

00:14:41.770 --> 00:14:46.510
Three months later, 200,000 North Korean troops crossed the 38th parallel.

00:14:47.350 --> 00:14:53.758
They invaded South Korea. The offensive was dazzling, but it was stopped dead in

00:14:53.758 --> 00:14:54.639
its tracks.

00:14:56.840 --> 00:15:00.833
What Kim Il-sung didn't understand at all was that Korea was the United States'

00:15:00.833 --> 00:15:02.349
protégé at the United Nations.

00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:07.953
They had a commitment to South Korea, not a security treaty, but at least a

00:15:07.953 --> 00:15:09.296
political commitment.

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:19.850
The United States quickly realized that this war was more than just a local war

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:25.690
and became, it must be said, a war between the 2 blocs.

00:15:28.390 --> 00:15:32.347
From the outset of the offensive, the American army was at the side of the South

00:15:32.347 --> 00:15:33.040
Korean forces.

00:15:34.290 --> 00:15:38.670
Kim Il-sung's troops were no match for the striking power of the US Air Force.

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:44.180
The Americans pushed them back and even entered North Korea.

00:15:46.480 --> 00:15:51.654
Kim Il-sung was not prepared for war with the Americans. When the US Air Force

00:15:51.654 --> 00:15:54.573
entered the scene, he didn't stand a chance.

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:59.340
But the North Korean leader still has a card to play.

00:16:00.540 --> 00:16:05.240
His powerful neighbor China did not appreciate this intrusion by the American army.

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:08.630
China then entered the conflict.

00:16:11.460 --> 00:16:16.080
The Chinese intervened when the Americans were getting very close to their border.

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:22.615
Hundreds of thousands of Chinese volunteers, in fact disguised soldiers,

00:16:22.615 --> 00:16:25.383
gradually pushed the Americans back.

00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:31.940
The Chinese intervention triggered panic in Washington, which stepped up its strikes.

00:16:33.070 --> 00:16:35.710
A deluge of fire rains down on North Korea.

00:16:41.710 --> 00:16:44.150
The destruction in North Korea was appalling.

00:16:44.950 --> 00:16:51.221
Civilians and entire villages were destroyed by the tons of napalm poured in by

00:16:51.221 --> 00:16:52.650
the American army.

00:16:56.284 --> 00:17:01.626
In Korea, the Americans used the same massive bombing strategy as in the Second

00:17:01.626 --> 00:17:02.302
World War.

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:05.670
They bombed everything they could.

00:17:06.730 --> 00:17:09.670
This caused deep psychological trauma.

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:17.530
At the end of the three-year war, North Korea was devastated.

00:17:19.780 --> 00:17:25.870
Three million dead, a border that had not moved and no peace treaty signed.

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:30.820
Kim Il-sung's attempted invasion failed.

00:17:33.917 --> 00:17:37.050
On the face of it, one might consider that Kim Il-sung had lost.

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:40.890
But not at all. For him, it's not a war that's over, it's a war that's going on.

00:17:41.110 --> 00:17:44.330
For the moment, it's a truce. But I'm going on. And one day, I'm going to win.

00:17:47.150 --> 00:17:48.890
For his dreams of greatness are still alive.

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:53.816
Unable to reign over a reunified Korea, he laid the foundations for a

00:17:53.816 --> 00:17:56.084
dictatorship in a devastated North Korea.

00:17:57.860 --> 00:18:00.240
This defeat was to become his strength.

00:18:05.510 --> 00:18:12.070
Thanks to the Korean War, he took absolute power. That was Kim Il-sung's victory.

00:18:13.780 --> 00:18:20.000
From Pyongyang in the late 50s, the nationalist leader established totalitarian power.

00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:27.320
The entire country was in a permanent state of mobilization. And paranoia set in.

00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:34.640
All opponents who could overshadow the regime had to be eliminated.

00:18:34.680 --> 00:18:40.940
The party embarks on an extraordinarily violent purge of all those under suspicion.

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:45.403
And it almost becomes a state law. It is estimated that nearly half a million

00:18:45.403 --> 00:18:46.445
people disappeared.

00:18:48.130 --> 00:18:52.200
To assert absolute power, Kim Il-sung created a military state.

00:18:53.580 --> 00:18:57.460
He set up several political police forces and brought the army to the forefront.

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:05.361
At the same time, a powerful propaganda machine was set up. The war had

00:19:05.361 --> 00:19:09.287
generated fears. The regime was going to exploit them.

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:14.741
The Americans who had ravaged the country were presented to the people as the

00:19:14.741 --> 00:19:15.505
worst enemies.

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:24.900
We've been taught this hatred since we were children.

00:19:27.300 --> 00:19:30.930
From childhood, North Koreans are taught that Americans are invaders.

00:19:32.950 --> 00:19:37.430
They are described in textbooks as barbarians who massacre innocent civilians.

00:19:39.450 --> 00:19:43.784
As a child, I thought the Americans were wolves, animals who take on the

00:19:43.784 --> 00:19:45.409
appearance of human beings.

00:19:47.670 --> 00:19:53.087
But the war nourished other resentments. Kim Il-sung has not forgotten the lack

00:19:53.087 --> 00:19:54.321
of Soviet support.

00:19:58.260 --> 00:20:02.908
On the surface, Kim Il-sung assures the Soviets that he is still a good friend.

00:20:02.908 --> 00:20:07.321
But behind the scenes, he is doing everything to increase his independence.

00:20:10.780 --> 00:20:17.640
To distance himself from Moscow, he invented a new form of communism in Korean

00:20:17.640 --> 00:20:18.872
colors: juche.

00:20:24.790 --> 00:20:30.975
The term juche simply means to be independent, to have a kind of character that

00:20:30.975 --> 00:20:33.011
allows you to go it alone.

00:20:33.090 --> 00:20:40.072
So it's a term linked to this idea of the Korean nation independent of the rest

00:20:40.072 --> 00:20:41.221
of the world.

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:49.580
One day, in a meeting, he explained this to the party members.

00:20:50.120 --> 00:20:54.732
The pro-Soviets want us to copy the Soviet model, the pro-Chinese want to

00:20:54.732 --> 00:20:55.616
imitate China.

00:20:56.340 --> 00:21:01.320
No, we have to build our revolution and our country in our own way.

00:21:02.930 --> 00:21:08.170
An autonomous and emancipated North Korea: an ambitious program.

00:21:09.210 --> 00:21:12.730
But the dictator still needs his Soviet allies.

00:21:17.030 --> 00:21:21.663
Since the war, the American army has left tens of thousands of soldiers on its

00:21:21.663 --> 00:21:22.910
bases in South Korea.

00:21:24.490 --> 00:21:28.304
Washington increased its deterrent presence by deploying short-range missiles

00:21:28.304 --> 00:21:29.840
equipped with nuclear warheads.

00:21:31.230 --> 00:21:38.870
By 1965, there were almost 750 warheads in South Korea, all aimed at the North.

00:21:43.020 --> 00:21:48.903
The Americans installed everything they needed to guard against any real

00:21:48.903 --> 00:21:51.518
invasion attempt from the North.

00:21:51.780 --> 00:21:57.225
The Americans considered and officially announced that South Korea was protected

00:21:57.225 --> 00:21:59.471
by the American nuclear umbrella.

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:07.270
We clearly threatened to use nuclear weapons during the Korean War.

00:22:08.730 --> 00:22:12.030
So it's not a theoretical threat in the minds of the North Koreans.

00:22:12.870 --> 00:22:16.478
At least two American presidents have threatened them with a nuclear bomb,

00:22:16.478 --> 00:22:18.721
although none of them actually carried it out.

00:22:20.480 --> 00:22:24.980
Kim Il-sung seized the opportunity to ask Moscow for the same protection.

00:22:33.200 --> 00:22:39.730
Kim Il-sung asked the Soviet Union to supply North Korea with missiles of

00:22:39.730 --> 00:22:44.650
comparable range and quality, but the Russians refused.

00:22:48.180 --> 00:22:52.402
Obviously, they were afraid of providing him with sophisticated weapons that

00:22:52.402 --> 00:22:55.624
they might use in the wrong way and for the wrong reasons.

00:22:59.052 --> 00:23:03.440
Once again, the Soviets disappointed the North Korean dictator.

00:23:04.940 --> 00:23:08.300
Kim Il-sung made atomic weapons his obsession.

00:23:09.780 --> 00:23:14.740
And since no one was willing to provide it, he tried to build it himself.

00:23:16.400 --> 00:23:23.380
Naturally, he was angry at his Soviet allies for refusing to help him with his project.

00:23:23.380 --> 00:23:30.140
So, using North Korean resources, he set out to develop an autonomous program.

00:23:37.010 --> 00:23:43.474
When Kim Il-sung began designing this program in the 60s, he believed that the

00:23:43.474 --> 00:23:46.127
next war would be a nuclear one.

00:23:49.910 --> 00:23:53.810
So he ordered all military bases moved underground.

00:23:55.720 --> 00:23:58.580
But his country had no nuclear experience.

00:23:59.740 --> 00:24:04.300
To make up for this, Kim Il-sung once again approached Moscow.

00:24:04.870 --> 00:24:09.690
He wants to obtain a civil nuclear reactor, the kind used to produce electricity.

00:24:11.390 --> 00:24:16.690
He won't be able to build his own bomb, but at least he'll have access to the technology.

00:24:19.150 --> 00:24:24.510
The Soviets choose to give them a tiny research reactor as a gesture of generosity.

00:24:27.250 --> 00:24:31.767
But it's very useful for the North Koreans, as they can start to learn the

00:24:31.767 --> 00:24:32.988
science of the atom.

00:24:35.470 --> 00:24:40.730
The reactor was designed for research and for exclusively peaceful use.

00:24:44.250 --> 00:24:49.490
In 1965, North Korea began its nuclear program in complete secrecy.

00:24:50.700 --> 00:24:54.040
But Kim Il-sung already knew that he would never see it through to the end.

00:25:01.890 --> 00:25:06.585
At the age of 58, the all-powerful dictator was worried about a tumor that had

00:25:06.585 --> 00:25:07.849
appeared in his neck.

00:25:09.330 --> 00:25:14.850
To ensure the continuity of his nuclear project, he must start preparing his succession.

00:25:15.997 --> 00:25:19.406
For Kim Il-sung, the problem is how to ensure the continuity of his regime.

00:25:19.491 --> 00:25:22.950
From the outset, he had considered a monarchical solution.

00:25:23.170 --> 00:25:26.795
The only solution was to have a leader who, like his predecessor, would maintain

00:25:26.795 --> 00:25:28.064
and even increase his power.

00:25:29.970 --> 00:25:34.419
To avoid an internal war that would weaken the regime, the patriarch came up

00:25:34.419 --> 00:25:37.171
with an idea unheard of in the Communist world.

00:25:39.233 --> 00:25:42.880
Pyongyang has become a backyard, with everyone dreaming of power.

00:25:42.930 --> 00:25:46.190
Anyone can take it, as long as they succeed.

00:25:46.213 --> 00:25:50.639
So when all allies are potential dangers, when anyone can betray him,

00:25:50.689 --> 00:25:53.720
he can only find someone in his family.

00:25:53.770 --> 00:25:57.750
Kim Il-sung has always been very loyal to his family.

00:25:59.570 --> 00:26:04.880
Unlike other communist leaders, he trusts only his family.

00:26:10.270 --> 00:26:16.150
Kim Il-sung has three sons. One of them will be entrusted with the reins of the country.

00:26:19.090 --> 00:26:23.400
Logic would dictate that it should be the eldest, Kim Jong-il. But the patriarch

00:26:23.400 --> 00:26:25.556
has trouble seeing him as his successor.

00:26:25.660 --> 00:26:29.687
Unlike his father, who is glorious, good-looking and always in a suit,

00:26:29.737 --> 00:26:32.259
in fact, he's always in boiler suits,

00:26:32.309 --> 00:26:35.823
he's short, poorly dressed.

00:26:38.110 --> 00:26:42.835
Kim Il-sung finds him ugly, he doesn't like him very much, he finds him too

00:26:42.835 --> 00:26:44.347
flattering, sycophantic.

00:26:44.530 --> 00:26:47.110
He doesn't trust him completely, he's suspicious of him.

00:26:48.050 --> 00:26:51.750
The old dictator especially disapproves of his eldest son's antics.

00:26:52.760 --> 00:26:54.100
It's all the palace talks about.

00:26:57.990 --> 00:27:03.510
They were drunken evenings with lots of very naked young women.

00:27:03.830 --> 00:27:08.110
A typical life of a prince, of an absolute monarchy.

00:27:08.110 --> 00:27:12.310
But at 28, Kim Jong-il dreams of succeeding his father.

00:27:13.630 --> 00:27:18.070
So he's going to do everything in his power to earn his father's trust.

00:27:30.020 --> 00:27:34.119
Kim Jong-il is always behind his father. He even ties his shoes, washes his

00:27:34.119 --> 00:27:36.305
feet, serves him food and cuts his meat.

00:27:36.740 --> 00:27:37.920
And the Koreans think that's great.

00:27:38.080 --> 00:27:42.735
It's become his trademark, in a way, to be in his father's shadow so that it

00:27:42.735 --> 00:27:43.898
affects his father.

00:27:45.510 --> 00:27:48.070
And his strategy doesn't stop there.

00:27:52.300 --> 00:27:54.520
Kim Jong-il is already working within the party.

00:27:55.440 --> 00:27:56.780
He's in charge of propaganda.

00:27:57.650 --> 00:28:01.930
He's going to set up a cult in his father's honor to flatter his ego.

00:28:10.610 --> 00:28:14.698
The Department of Propaganda and Agitation is one of the most powerful

00:28:14.698 --> 00:28:17.851
departments, in charge of managing the leader's image.

00:28:20.140 --> 00:28:24.840
Kim Jong-il's father worship is hysterical.

00:28:25.340 --> 00:28:30.020
Statues are everywhere. There are, it seems, 30,000 statues of him all over the country.

00:28:30.240 --> 00:28:33.180
An infinite cult of personality.

00:28:33.600 --> 00:28:37.280
Everything is renamed Kim Il-sung. The country became Kim Il-sung country.

00:28:43.760 --> 00:28:48.660
We learn about Kim Il-sung's childhood in elementary school, his adolescence in

00:28:48.660 --> 00:28:50.397
junior high and high school.

00:28:52.500 --> 00:28:59.257
We grow up with his revolutionary past. When you finish school, that's the end

00:28:59.257 --> 00:29:01.163
of the indoctrination.

00:29:04.070 --> 00:29:09.550
At that point, we no longer think of him as a human being, but as a god.

00:29:14.560 --> 00:29:20.720
The first sentence I learned to write was "Thank you father Kim Il-sung".

00:29:21.610 --> 00:29:25.830
After that, I learned to write my name and my parents' names.

00:29:26.510 --> 00:29:28.310
And it was the same for everyone.

00:29:30.290 --> 00:29:35.430
Everyone in North Korea thought Kim Il-sung was a god who lived above mankind.

00:29:38.550 --> 00:29:41.990
If you call Kim Il-sung by his proper name, you must die.

00:29:43.290 --> 00:29:48.300
Always add a qualifier in front of his name, such as "glorious leader". If you

00:29:48.300 --> 00:29:52.025
just say his name, you're considered a political criminal.

00:29:54.560 --> 00:29:58.540
Four years later, Kim Jong-il's plan has borne fruit.

00:30:00.050 --> 00:30:04.830
His father, who had survived the mood, had just chosen him as his successor.

00:30:15.610 --> 00:30:22.324
From February 1974 onwards, the media started talking about Kim Jong-il as the

00:30:22.324 --> 00:30:23.443
party leader.

00:30:26.490 --> 00:30:28.910
This meant that he was the successor.

00:30:30.090 --> 00:30:32.110
But nothing was known about him.

00:30:36.230 --> 00:30:40.105
Kim Il-sung would remain at the head of the country until his death, but he

00:30:40.105 --> 00:30:42.068
entrusted internal affairs to his son.

00:30:43.350 --> 00:30:47.035
At the age of 32, Kim Jong-il had to demonstrate his ability to ensure the

00:30:47.035 --> 00:30:48.280
continuity of the regime.

00:30:52.910 --> 00:30:57.720
That year, the North Korean economy was hit hard by the oil crisis.

00:30:59.110 --> 00:31:00.930
And it was up to him to find a solution.

00:31:04.010 --> 00:31:07.390
Within six months, North Korea was almost bankrupt.

00:31:08.670 --> 00:31:13.082
It could no longer repay its loans, it was running out of cash, and banks were

00:31:13.082 --> 00:31:14.553
no longer willing to lend.

00:31:18.810 --> 00:31:23.563
At the same time, Kim Jong-il realized that if he ever wanted to take the reins

00:31:23.563 --> 00:31:25.729
of power, the regime had to survive.

00:31:26.430 --> 00:31:29.370
Otherwise, there's no future for him and his family.

00:31:31.770 --> 00:31:37.677
He realizes that it's essential to raise cash at a time when the whole economy

00:31:37.677 --> 00:31:39.874
is on the verge of imploding.

00:31:40.590 --> 00:31:46.233
To boost the coffers, Kim Jong-il decides to create a secret administration,

00:31:46.233 --> 00:31:46.975
Bureau 39.

00:31:48.280 --> 00:31:52.080
Its mission was to find money, wherever it came from.

00:31:59.490 --> 00:32:05.230
They use the expression "catching dollars in the air".

00:32:05.230 --> 00:32:12.230
This meant exploiting every possible avenue to find hard currency.

00:32:13.590 --> 00:32:20.430
Bureau 39 controlled all exports,

00:32:21.840 --> 00:32:28.410
such as industrial production, freight forwarding and even gold bullion production.

00:32:30.010 --> 00:32:32.890
They ran all North Korea's most lucrative businesses.

00:32:38.160 --> 00:32:44.430
And the most lucrative business for Kim Jong-il was international drug trafficking.

00:32:44.890 --> 00:32:50.390
They were very creative. They got into organized crime on a massive scale.

00:32:51.290 --> 00:32:56.706
It's very interesting, and it mainly involved the production and distribution of

00:32:56.706 --> 00:32:58.602
hard drugs around the world.

00:33:01.400 --> 00:33:05.203
The North Koreans do business without asking too many questions about what is

00:33:05.203 --> 00:33:06.290
legal and what is not.

00:33:08.140 --> 00:33:09.740
For them, everything is legal.

00:33:19.270 --> 00:33:25.430
On Kim Jong-il's orders, all the mountain villages are now growing poppies,

00:33:27.330 --> 00:33:30.890
the basic ingredient for producing opium and heroin.

00:33:33.110 --> 00:33:35.490
The whole population is put to work.

00:33:36.680 --> 00:33:43.340
You have whole towns whose entire economy is based on this production.

00:33:43.840 --> 00:33:50.580
Where school-age children are taken to the fields to help with the harvest.

00:33:53.780 --> 00:33:59.180
Even soldiers are often used as labor to help produce opium.

00:34:05.150 --> 00:34:08.230
It was called the White Campanula farm.

00:34:09.790 --> 00:34:14.670
We were stationed there in turn for three months to harvest poppy flowers.

00:34:15.510 --> 00:34:16.930
I actually harvested poppies.

00:34:17.810 --> 00:34:19.490
It was a big opium farm.

00:34:20.350 --> 00:34:23.530
At the time, I didn't know that selling opium was illegal.

00:34:27.410 --> 00:34:30.530
That's just the tip of the iceberg.

00:34:31.190 --> 00:34:36.998
In fact, producing drugs is easy, especially when you control the police forces

00:34:36.998 --> 00:34:38.616
and state authorities.

00:34:39.110 --> 00:34:44.192
What's difficult is smuggling it abroad, bringing back the proceeds and

00:34:44.192 --> 00:34:45.338
laundering them.

00:34:47.900 --> 00:34:52.910
To move the merchandise and repatriate the dirty money, Bureau 39 coordinates

00:34:52.910 --> 00:34:56.294
all the state services involved in drug trafficking.

00:35:08.435 --> 00:35:14.290
At the time, the easiest way to distribute drugs was through the diplomatic corps.

00:35:16.690 --> 00:35:22.115
A diplomat has immunity, which means that a foreign government has no right to

00:35:22.115 --> 00:35:22.880
search him.

00:35:24.870 --> 00:35:31.138
This also applies to their luggage. These suitcases are the property of the

00:35:31.138 --> 00:35:32.726
North Korean state.

00:35:38.460 --> 00:35:44.584
Little by little, in the 70s and 80s, North Korea's diplomatic network became

00:35:44.584 --> 00:35:50.469
the regime's main channel for exporting drugs around the world and earning

00:35:50.469 --> 00:35:51.821
foreign currency.

00:35:58.290 --> 00:36:03.015
The profits are difficult to estimate, but must have been in the region of $40

00:36:03.015 --> 00:36:04.409
million every 6 months.

00:36:09.330 --> 00:36:14.455
If there were a university of organized crime, there would be books explaining

00:36:14.455 --> 00:36:17.084
how the North Korean government does it.

00:36:21.970 --> 00:36:26.753
Thanks to the opium and heroin trade, Kim Jong-il is becoming considerably

00:36:26.753 --> 00:36:29.985
richer, enabling the regime to survive the crisis.

00:36:33.338 --> 00:36:37.890
But above all, he prepared for his accession to power by buying off the

00:36:37.890 --> 00:36:39.685
country's powerful families.

00:36:45.510 --> 00:36:51.392
In 1976, for the party's 30th anniversary, 5,000 cadres received Japanese

00:36:51.392 --> 00:36:56.629
refrigerators and luxury watches bearing Kim Il-sung's signature.

00:37:01.530 --> 00:37:07.642
Everyone knew it was Kim Jong-il who was organizing all this. He was discreetly

00:37:07.642 --> 00:37:09.422
reinforcing his status.

00:37:13.200 --> 00:37:18.918
Kim Jong-il built his power alongside his father. Kim Il-sung let him do so, at

00:37:18.918 --> 00:37:22.827
least in part, to ensure a smooth transition of power.

00:37:23.840 --> 00:37:29.114
In the early 1980s, the two Kims held the country. While the son ran the mafia

00:37:29.114 --> 00:37:33.172
organization, the father pursued his secret nuclear program.

00:37:40.570 --> 00:37:45.238
In 15 years, the North Koreans have never succeeded in building a bomb using the

00:37:45.238 --> 00:37:47.631
civilian reactor supplied by the Soviets.

00:37:48.370 --> 00:37:53.226
But they have just found plans in British archives that should enable them to

00:37:53.226 --> 00:37:55.686
build a new one, of a different design.

00:37:57.870 --> 00:38:04.110
These plans were freely available. The North Koreans had managed to obtain all

00:38:04.110 --> 00:38:06.350
the construction parameters.

00:38:16.140 --> 00:38:21.589
The North Koreans have a very good reason for choosing this type of reactor,

00:38:21.589 --> 00:38:27.111
because they have natural uranium. They have enormous uranium resources. They

00:38:27.111 --> 00:38:29.836
don't need to import fuel from abroad.

00:38:42.910 --> 00:38:48.318
This type of reactor can be used for both civil and military purposes, because

00:38:48.318 --> 00:38:54.280
if you take the nuclear fuel out and process it, then you can potentially make a bomb.

00:38:57.320 --> 00:39:02.940
This time, the North Koreans are going to move forward in disguise. In 1985,

00:39:02.940 --> 00:39:07.673
under pressure from the Soviets, they agreed to sign the Nuclear

00:39:07.673 --> 00:39:09.522
Non-Proliferation Treaty.

00:39:10.880 --> 00:39:16.780
But on the Yongbyon site, they built the new reactor that would finally enable

00:39:16.780 --> 00:39:18.444
them to have the bomb.

00:39:25.780 --> 00:39:30.713
In the early 90s, the Soviet Union collapsed. The bipolar world inherited from

00:39:30.713 --> 00:39:35.456
the Second World War disappeared, and North Korea lost its Soviet guardian.

00:39:35.520 --> 00:39:39.551
Feeling isolated on the international stage, Kim Il-sung wanted to reassure the

00:39:39.551 --> 00:39:40.928
world on the nuclear front.

00:39:41.080 --> 00:39:45.339
He accepted a visit from inspectors from the IAEA, the International Atomic

00:39:45.339 --> 00:39:49.883
Energy Agency set up by the United Nations to monitor nuclear non-proliferation.

00:39:50.300 --> 00:39:54.823
Kim Il-sung knows full well that he is not complying with the treaty he has

00:39:54.823 --> 00:39:59.527
signed, but he is convinced that his military installations are so well hidden

00:39:59.527 --> 00:40:01.819
that the IAEA will not notice a thing.

00:40:04.600 --> 00:40:11.582
In May 1992, an IAEA delegation visited North Korea's nuclear facilities for the

00:40:11.582 --> 00:40:12.542
first time.

00:40:13.790 --> 00:40:18.878
Heading the delegation was the Director of the international agency, Hans Blix,

00:40:18.878 --> 00:40:24.225
who had come to see for himself whether the plant was indeed producing electricity.

00:40:32.150 --> 00:40:36.470
The Yongbyon site is surrounded by concrete walls and iron gates.

00:40:39.070 --> 00:40:42.350
The technology used on site is old but effective.

00:40:49.150 --> 00:40:53.962
They have old equipment dating back to the 50s and 60s, in other words, to the

00:40:53.962 --> 00:40:55.628
time when they acquired it.

00:40:56.970 --> 00:41:01.695
But the reactor itself and the equipment to manufacture the nuclear material,

00:41:01.695 --> 00:41:05.868
even if it would never pass safety standards, are highly functional.

00:41:10.070 --> 00:41:14.770
The North Korean engineers are proud to present their nuclear technology.

00:41:15.840 --> 00:41:20.540
They show Hans Blix the reactor core, which has been in operation for 6 years.

00:41:27.177 --> 00:41:32.744
The tour continues to the cooling pool. Despite the dilapidated state of the

00:41:32.744 --> 00:41:36.406
equipment, everything is in perfect working order.

00:41:38.730 --> 00:41:42.370
At the end of his visit, Hans Blix can't get over it.

00:41:43.682 --> 00:41:50.853
We're impressed by the engineers' ability to build their own

00:41:51.152 --> 00:41:58.399
have managed to build their reactor all by themselves.

00:41:59.280 --> 00:42:04.336
When the experts leave, the North Koreans are confident. They have succeeded in

00:42:04.336 --> 00:42:06.576
concealing their military activity.

00:42:07.340 --> 00:42:12.420
A clandestine waste reprocessing plant, of course, which they hid from the inspectors.

00:42:14.190 --> 00:42:19.910
Before we received the inspectors in 1992, we had hidden all the nuclear equipment.

00:42:21.690 --> 00:42:23.850
I was vice-president of the waste treatment plant.

00:42:25.710 --> 00:42:30.004
We covered certain parts of the plant with lead sheets, because lead blocks

00:42:30.004 --> 00:42:34.412
radioactivity, which would prevent the group of inspectors from measuring it.

00:42:37.020 --> 00:42:42.020
But two months later, a new team of IAEA inspectors was sent to the site.

00:42:42.240 --> 00:42:47.230
This time, to take samples and carry out precise analyses that the North Koreans

00:42:47.230 --> 00:42:48.477
had not anticipated.

00:42:52.920 --> 00:42:58.817
In 1992, we had new tools at the IAEA. This new verification method was based on

00:42:58.817 --> 00:43:01.766
the collection of environmental samples.

00:43:07.790 --> 00:43:11.310
Using absorbent cotton, we collected dust deposited on surfaces.

00:43:13.330 --> 00:43:16.790
It contained minute particles of uranium and plutonium.

00:43:24.740 --> 00:43:30.460
I think they were caught off guard because we were using these new investigative methods.

00:43:31.240 --> 00:43:35.660
They didn't know about it. That's when the problems started.

00:43:37.600 --> 00:43:43.104
And these analyses reveal that the North Koreans are secretly reprocessing their

00:43:43.104 --> 00:43:46.131
nuclear waste. A totally forbidden practice.

00:43:46.200 --> 00:43:51.563
If you have a reprocessing plant, it's a sign that you want plutonium. And why

00:43:51.563 --> 00:43:55.551
do you need plutonium to make bombs? It was very alarming.

00:43:57.380 --> 00:44:03.740
That's why we had no choice but to take it to the UN Security Council.

00:44:09.420 --> 00:44:13.678
For Washington, these revelations are proof that the North Koreans do indeed

00:44:13.678 --> 00:44:16.143
have a clandestine factory for military use.

00:44:17.050 --> 00:44:19.570
The CIA had had doubts for years.

00:44:25.370 --> 00:44:31.049
As early as 1986, satellite photos showed something resembling the foundations

00:44:31.049 --> 00:44:32.797
of a reprocessing plant.

00:44:34.970 --> 00:44:38.430
You could see trenches between sites that had no reason to be connected.

00:44:39.150 --> 00:44:42.570
You could also see tanks that were to be used to store waste.

00:44:44.430 --> 00:44:46.090
Washington set conditions.

00:44:46.830 --> 00:44:51.160
The North Koreans would no longer be able to handle their nuclear waste without

00:44:51.160 --> 00:44:52.695
the presence of IAEA agents.

00:44:57.850 --> 00:45:03.782
If they removed this fuel to make plutonium, they would have had enough to build

00:45:03.782 --> 00:45:04.375
6 bombs.

00:45:05.170 --> 00:45:06.890
For us, this was a very serious problem.

00:45:12.930 --> 00:45:17.720
We had already informed the North Koreans that if they started reprocessing this

00:45:17.720 --> 00:45:22.810
fuel, in other words, recovering the plutonium, this would have serious consequences.

00:45:24.610 --> 00:45:28.739
But the North Koreans did not heed these injunctions and continued the

00:45:28.739 --> 00:45:31.571
clandestine reprocessing of their nuclear waste.

00:45:33.310 --> 00:45:39.030
On the other hand, they decided to stop hiding. On the contrary, their nuclear

00:45:39.030 --> 00:45:42.476
program will become their weapon of deterrence.

00:45:46.840 --> 00:45:52.017
We threatened them with very heavy sanctions if they continued. They told us

00:45:52.017 --> 00:45:56.581
that if we imposed sanctions, they would consider it an act of war.

00:45:57.760 --> 00:45:59.080
Very explicit terms.

00:46:01.190 --> 00:46:04.350
They threatened to turn Seoul into a sea of flames.

00:46:06.750 --> 00:46:08.090
It was a very serious crisis.

00:46:08.710 --> 00:46:13.470
It was my first issue as Secretary of Defense, the prospect of war.

00:46:14.230 --> 00:46:19.830
The situation between the United States and North Korea was escalating rapidly.

00:46:20.470 --> 00:46:22.470
It was getting out of control.

00:46:24.510 --> 00:46:28.484
The North Koreans' provocations seemed to be leading them straight into a new

00:46:28.484 --> 00:46:29.878
war with the United States.

00:46:33.900 --> 00:46:38.320
It was then that former president Jimmy Carter offered his services to the White House.

00:46:39.140 --> 00:46:44.000
He wanted to go to Pyongyang to try to open negotiations with the North Korean leaders.

00:46:48.150 --> 00:46:52.290
We had no formal discussions, no embassy in Pyongyang.

00:46:53.130 --> 00:46:55.050
No way to communicate directly.

00:46:56.270 --> 00:47:01.530
So the President authorized Carter to go to Pyongyang to talk with Kim Il-sung.

00:47:02.380 --> 00:47:06.540
President Clinton agreed to let Carter intervene.

00:47:07.540 --> 00:47:11.640
But at the same time, he launched preparations for military intervention.

00:47:22.980 --> 00:47:29.021
On June 15, Jimmy Carter and his wife arrived at the DMZ, the demilitarized zone

00:47:29.021 --> 00:47:30.984
separating the two Koreas.

00:47:32.130 --> 00:47:36.230
They crossed the border on foot, surrounded by secret service agents.

00:47:38.940 --> 00:47:41.600
A delegation from Pyongyang had come to welcome them.

00:47:43.350 --> 00:47:48.270
It was the first time an American president had set foot on North Korean soil.

00:47:50.430 --> 00:47:59.050
These images of Carter crossing the DMZ, it's a proud feeling to be on an equal footing,

00:47:59.170 --> 00:48:03.630
to have an American president come directly to North Korea.

00:48:04.830 --> 00:48:09.990
The next day, Jimmy Carter met Kim Il-sung at the presidential palace.

00:48:13.680 --> 00:48:16.950
The handshake was historic.

00:48:20.690 --> 00:48:24.610
In Pyongyang, they ate meals together and visited the city and its monuments.

00:48:25.590 --> 00:48:29.130
But Carter hadn't come to visit the country with the North Korean leaders.

00:48:29.830 --> 00:48:31.770
What he wanted was to avoid war.

00:48:32.510 --> 00:48:38.070
He was trying to use these moments of socialization to find a solution to the problem.

00:48:39.690 --> 00:48:44.720
Carter complied with protocol, but he knew he didn't have much time to negotiate.

00:48:45.370 --> 00:48:50.810
11,000 kilometers away, President Clinton is about to launch a military intervention.

00:48:55.170 --> 00:49:00.300
Preparations have been underway at the White House since early this morning.

00:49:01.450 --> 00:49:03.630
And intervention is imminent.

00:49:04.290 --> 00:49:09.012
I was in the Situation Room briefing the President and the entire national

00:49:09.012 --> 00:49:09.906
security team.

00:49:11.070 --> 00:49:14.310
We had no way of assessing what Kim Il-sung had in mind,

00:49:15.270 --> 00:49:19.250
but we thought there was a reasonable chance he would carry out these threats.

00:49:23.960 --> 00:49:28.020
We really wanted President Carter to succeed in defusing the crisis.

00:49:28.620 --> 00:49:31.480
But at the same time, we couldn't be sure of his success,

00:49:31.960 --> 00:49:34.600
and we needed to take preventive measures.

00:49:36.580 --> 00:49:39.700
So we had to be ready before imposing sanctions.

00:49:40.720 --> 00:49:44.660
And I suggested sending an extra 30,000 troops to South Korea.

00:49:45.760 --> 00:49:48.940
That would have been a very important and provocative maneuver.

00:49:54.690 --> 00:50:00.170
There was also the option of destroying Yongbyon before it could produce atomic bombs.

00:50:00.590 --> 00:50:03.890
We had a chance to stop their nuclear program before it began in earnest.

00:50:04.710 --> 00:50:07.368
Because everything was right in front of our eyes at Yongbyon.

00:50:07.490 --> 00:50:10.057
The reactor, the fuel rods, everything was there.

00:50:11.500 --> 00:50:13.120
President Clinton hesitated.

00:50:14.460 --> 00:50:17.760
Any military action would lead to retaliation by the North Koreans.

00:50:18.930 --> 00:50:21.210
And the consequences would be dramatic.

00:50:27.424 --> 00:50:31.570
The worry, of course, was that the North Koreans would use their artillery,

00:50:32.370 --> 00:50:34.430
hidden in underground tunnels along the demilitarized zone,

00:50:35.750 --> 00:50:39.250
to destroy Seoul, a city of over 11 million inhabitants.

00:50:39.930 --> 00:50:41.730
This would have caused enormous damage.

00:50:44.950 --> 00:50:49.350
General Locke estimated that a new Korean War would result in a million casualties,

00:50:49.690 --> 00:50:51.930
and more than a billion dollars in material damage.

00:50:53.160 --> 00:50:57.900
And this is where Jimmy Carter, in a way, fell from the sky.

00:51:00.220 --> 00:51:03.260
Just as President Clinton was about to make his decision,

00:51:04.170 --> 00:51:05.610
he received an urgent message.

00:51:06.700 --> 00:51:09.380
Former President Carter is on the line.

00:51:11.700 --> 00:51:15.360
We were in the process of presenting options to the president,

00:51:16.220 --> 00:51:18.120
when a call came in from Pyongyang,

00:51:18.920 --> 00:51:20.900
saying the North Koreans were ready to talk.

00:51:21.900 --> 00:51:25.880
They knew we were meeting, and that it was the right time to get their message across.

00:51:27.170 --> 00:51:30.030
There was no way the timing was a coincidence.

00:51:30.910 --> 00:51:34.810
Our meeting had been going on for an hour, and the call came just then.

00:51:42.130 --> 00:51:44.750
The president asked me to answer the call,

00:51:45.170 --> 00:51:48.670
and so I went into a very small room, a sort of phone booth,

00:51:49.450 --> 00:51:52.210
and had a conversation with former President Jimmy Carter.

00:51:52.670 --> 00:51:55.370
He described to me what he thought he'd gotten.

00:51:56.710 --> 00:52:01.550
Carter would have gotten Kim Il-sung to promise to stop reprocessing nuclear waste.

00:52:02.770 --> 00:52:05.370
Apparently, all the North Koreans wanted,

00:52:05.830 --> 00:52:07.450
was to open negotiations.

00:52:11.690 --> 00:52:16.010
They felt they could negotiate a deal with the West, and even more so with the Americans.

00:52:16.570 --> 00:52:18.830
The United States would become their sponsor, their protector.

00:52:25.900 --> 00:52:27.420
There was a great deal of tension.

00:52:28.260 --> 00:52:32.820
First, the meeting was interrupted by Pyongyang's appeal, then our conditions

00:52:32.820 --> 00:52:37.557
stipulating that North Korea had to commit to stopping waste reprocessing before

00:52:37.557 --> 00:52:39.097
the end of our discussion,

00:52:39.580 --> 00:52:41.560
and the final answer was yes.

00:52:47.500 --> 00:52:49.560
The Americans had approached the precipice.

00:52:50.460 --> 00:52:53.980
They had foreseen the disaster that lay ahead if they went through with their logic.

00:52:54.240 --> 00:52:58.040
And Jimmy Carter saved us from ourselves.

00:52:59.840 --> 00:53:03.864
The meeting was adjourned because the idea of sending 30,000 troops to Seoul was

00:53:03.864 --> 00:53:04.769
becoming obsolete.

00:53:14.340 --> 00:53:16.860
Kim Il-sung has no intention of stopping his program.

00:53:17.900 --> 00:53:21.980
But by making false promises to the Americans, he has bought himself some time.

00:53:23.520 --> 00:53:26.080
On the other hand, he has another problem to deal with.

00:53:26.940 --> 00:53:30.667
He has just realized that his son Kim Jong-il has been lying to him about the

00:53:30.667 --> 00:53:32.071
country's economic situation.

00:53:33.404 --> 00:53:38.018
Despite the various businesses he has set up over the past 20 years, the coffers

00:53:38.018 --> 00:53:38.595
are empty.

00:53:38.857 --> 00:53:42.890
The old patriarch, obsessed with his bomb, never saw it coming.

00:53:43.900 --> 00:53:48.120
Kim Il-sung had decided to return to business.

00:53:49.300 --> 00:53:52.960
And then he discovered that the North Korean economy was in meltdown.

00:53:54.380 --> 00:53:56.280
He hadn't realized it until now.

00:54:02.080 --> 00:54:07.440
Kim Il-sung realized that many factories were not operating normally.

00:54:09.820 --> 00:54:13.680
There was also a problem with food distribution in the country.

00:54:16.300 --> 00:54:17.420
It was no longer guaranteed.

00:54:19.620 --> 00:54:22.040
Kim Il-sung was very disappointed and disillusioned.

00:54:41.550 --> 00:54:44.850
Kim Il-sung dismissed all Kim Jong-il's men.

00:54:47.650 --> 00:54:52.310
He took charge and wanted to receive all reports on North Korea directly.

00:54:54.730 --> 00:54:59.030
From then on, the relationship between father and son deteriorated sharply.

00:55:05.070 --> 00:55:08.370
That day, father and son had to talk on the phone.

00:55:08.870 --> 00:55:10.590
And the conversation goes awry.

00:55:10.590 --> 00:55:19.330
It is alleged that he had a fit of rage, that he cursed his son devilishly,

00:55:19.770 --> 00:55:24.790
that he threatened to take away his power, and then that he lost his temper and

00:55:24.790 --> 00:55:25.426
fell down.

00:55:26.330 --> 00:55:30.971
At the age of 82, in the middle of an argument with his son, Kim Il-sung

00:55:30.971 --> 00:55:32.905
collapsed from a heart attack.

00:55:35.580 --> 00:55:38.960
He disappeared, dreadful. He's been around for 50 years.

00:55:39.260 --> 00:55:42.854
It was an unimaginable tragedy for the population, who, deep down, had never

00:55:42.854 --> 00:55:44.272
known anything like it before.

00:55:53.270 --> 00:55:58.990
A few days later, the tribute paid to the dictator was the height of the regime.

00:56:01.330 --> 00:56:07.830
For 10 hours, the funeral cortege marched 40 km in front of a huge crowd.

00:56:15.330 --> 00:56:18.910
We learned about it from the media. At first, we couldn't believe it.

00:56:20.010 --> 00:56:22.670
How can a god die? A god doesn't die.

00:56:28.730 --> 00:56:31.750
The North Korean people were stunned.

00:56:34.250 --> 00:56:37.890
So the top brass sent women to weep.

00:56:45.850 --> 00:56:50.890
And when they started sobbing, people empathized.

00:56:52.190 --> 00:56:55.450
We all became sad when we saw all those women in tears.

00:56:57.330 --> 00:56:59.310
And we started crying too.

00:56:59.310 --> 00:57:13.170
When we heard of his death, everyone was shocked.

00:57:13.910 --> 00:57:17.450
I was upset, as if I'd lost my own father.

00:57:18.050 --> 00:57:19.310
I cried for several days.

00:57:33.470 --> 00:57:35.650
Kim Il-sung's body is embalmed.

00:57:35.970 --> 00:57:40.090
It costs astronomical sums, we're talking about 10 million dollars, crazy things.

00:57:40.510 --> 00:57:44.730
It's on display in the palace, which has been completely refurbished, with

00:57:44.730 --> 00:57:48.892
absolutely extraordinary measures. You have to queue for hours to get in.

00:57:49.110 --> 00:57:53.353
You have to go through cameras. And if you're completely decontaminated, no dust

00:57:53.353 --> 00:57:53.936
can get in.

00:57:54.290 --> 00:57:55.730
They tell you how to stand.

00:57:56.010 --> 00:58:00.310
You can watch for half a minute, and then we pass Kim Il-sung's catafalque.

00:58:03.330 --> 00:58:06.230
Kim Il-sung was like the sun for the people.

00:58:06.950 --> 00:58:11.770
But when the sun suddenly disappeared, the world went dark.

00:58:12.250 --> 00:58:14.970
North Koreans were completely disoriented.

00:58:18.190 --> 00:58:19.490
Kim Il-sung died.

00:58:21.320 --> 00:58:27.460
At the age of 52, his son, Kim Jong-il, could at last officially assume absolute power.

00:58:28.610 --> 00:58:32.090
The North Korean population hadn't seen much of him.

00:58:33.290 --> 00:58:37.884
They had only heard his voice for 12 seconds during a military parade in the

00:58:37.884 --> 00:58:38.489
early 90s.

00:58:39.860 --> 00:58:42.820
He was a kind of mysterious figure who took power.

00:58:46.140 --> 00:58:50.513
Kim Jong-il, of course, makes it clear that from now on, he's in charge, and

00:58:50.513 --> 00:58:51.722
he's in charge alone.

00:58:51.900 --> 00:58:53.880
He is now the new Kim Il-sung.

00:58:59.300 --> 00:59:02.680
With the death of Kim Il-sung, the international community began to wonder.

00:59:02.860 --> 00:59:07.755
Will his successor, Kim Jong-il, have the same nuclear obsession? Or will he

00:59:07.755 --> 00:59:12.715
respect the promise his father had made to Jimmy Carter a few months earlier?

00:59:12.780 --> 00:59:16.660
After years of anti-American propaganda, nothing is less certain.

00:59:16.660 --> 00:59:21.657
In any case, his priority at the moment is to find a way to revive his country,

00:59:21.657 --> 00:59:22.796
which is in ruins.

00:59:26.030 --> 00:59:30.960
In 1994, Kim Jong-il inherited a country he himself had brought to its knees.

00:59:33.810 --> 00:59:37.848
During his years at the helm, he had enriched the country's top dignitaries and

00:59:37.848 --> 00:59:38.308
the army.

00:59:39.590 --> 00:59:42.870
But he had also considerably impoverished the population.

00:59:44.770 --> 00:59:46.570
Everything collapsed the year he came to power.

00:59:47.830 --> 00:59:51.650
Within months, the country was hit by an unprecedented famine.

00:59:53.610 --> 00:59:57.170
If there had been markets, people could have survived.

00:59:58.250 --> 00:59:59.610
But there weren't even any markets any more.

01:00:02.390 --> 01:00:06.410
The state was the sole provider of food for the North Korean people.

01:00:10.530 --> 01:00:14.450
They couldn't imagine the government starving them out.

01:00:16.130 --> 01:00:18.170
So they waited for the food rations.

01:00:19.510 --> 01:00:21.650
And they all starved to death waiting.

01:00:30.530 --> 01:00:35.790
The abandoned children, the starving, it all happened at once.

01:00:36.650 --> 01:00:37.230
Like war.

01:00:38.290 --> 01:00:39.530
It didn't happen gradually.

01:00:40.470 --> 01:00:43.010
It was a brutal change in people's daily lives.

01:00:43.730 --> 01:00:46.310
People were thrown into a state of panic by it.

01:00:51.690 --> 01:00:53.770
There were so many dead bodies.

01:00:54.690 --> 01:00:56.990
People came to collect them and bury them.

01:00:58.290 --> 01:01:01.790
In mountainous regions, meals were offered for this work.

01:01:02.650 --> 01:01:05.250
They were called 827 carts.

01:01:06.950 --> 01:01:10.570
In the summer of 1995, isolated and cornered,

01:01:11.490 --> 01:01:15.630
Kim Jong-il decided to open his country to international aid for the first time.

01:01:18.160 --> 01:01:23.308
He had no choice. He had to let in foreign NGOs to avoid the total collapse of

01:01:23.308 --> 01:01:24.034
his regime.

01:01:25.490 --> 01:01:28.190
One evening, we received a written message by fax,

01:01:28.190 --> 01:01:35.950
telling us that the North Korean authorities were inviting us to work in their country.

01:01:36.530 --> 01:01:38.550
We were obviously completely stunned.

01:01:38.890 --> 01:01:46.445
This was the last thing we expected, given the North Korean regime's reputation

01:01:46.445 --> 01:01:48.454
for absolute closure.

01:01:48.550 --> 01:01:53.990
We knew that children were starving to death.

01:01:55.040 --> 01:01:56.560
The question was raised.

01:01:57.140 --> 01:02:01.400
Could we let children, innocent people, starve to death? We had a moral

01:02:01.400 --> 01:02:04.100
obligation to intervene, whatever the regime.

01:02:06.060 --> 01:02:08.940
North Korea is becoming the most assisted country in the world.

01:02:09.910 --> 01:02:11.970
All the humanitarian organizations are there.

01:02:13.570 --> 01:02:16.050
Aid worth billions of dollars.

01:02:18.050 --> 01:02:21.430
These were huge budgets. The bulk was rice, of course.

01:02:21.710 --> 01:02:29.007
Absolutely enormous quantities, capable of providing the regime with a very

01:02:29.007 --> 01:02:30.272
clear crutch.

01:02:30.670 --> 01:02:34.050
At that point, North Korea could have collapsed.

01:02:36.470 --> 01:02:38.990
The pressure on the regime was incredible.

01:02:39.760 --> 01:02:43.320
But they received outside help, and that undoubtedly saved them.

01:02:46.140 --> 01:02:52.110
But while his country was dying, the dictator kept his family in opulence.

01:02:53.820 --> 01:02:55.540
His children have grown up in the greatest secrecy.

01:02:56.830 --> 01:03:00.070
Particularly his three sons, born of extramarital relationships.

01:03:02.470 --> 01:03:07.650
The youngest, Kim Jong-un, is the child of his fourth mistress.

01:03:09.930 --> 01:03:16.270
In the 90s, nobody knew Kim Jong-un, including those in power.

01:03:18.010 --> 01:03:21.030
Nobody knew who he was, his name didn't exist.

01:03:25.110 --> 01:03:27.390
Kim Jong-un was not allowed to meet anyone.

01:03:28.670 --> 01:03:30.650
No one was supposed to know who his mother was.

01:03:31.646 --> 01:03:33.050
Why not?

01:03:33.050 --> 01:03:34.430
Because she wasn't the legitimate wife.

01:03:35.510 --> 01:03:36.650
She couldn't appear.

01:03:37.870 --> 01:03:41.820
No one was allowed to meet the hidden members of the Kim family.

01:03:46.550 --> 01:03:54.770
The executives and family entourage didn't dare treat him like a child his own age.

01:03:56.990 --> 01:04:02.170
They couldn't be familiar with him because he might be the next leader.

01:04:07.520 --> 01:04:13.864
Kim Jong-un had a huge room full of toys, but no friends. When he went to

01:04:13.864 --> 01:04:16.993
school, his teachers were terrified,

01:04:18.060 --> 01:04:21.400
like in those movies where a child can kill you with a look.

01:04:22.940 --> 01:04:26.280
Kim Jong-il realized that this was not healthy for a child.

01:04:29.110 --> 01:04:33.290
So the dictator decided to send Kim Jong-un abroad to study,

01:04:34.830 --> 01:04:38.520
in a country where secrets are closely guarded: Switzerland.

01:04:41.550 --> 01:04:44.979
Switzerland is considered by many absolute monarchies to be the "nec plus

01:04:44.979 --> 01:04:48.643
ultra", where you get a good education and don't get asked too many questions.

01:04:49.710 --> 01:04:52.810
He wanted his children to live out their youth like everyone else,

01:04:53.150 --> 01:04:59.270
let them have friends, because it's an age when politics are not yet discussed.

01:05:04.930 --> 01:05:11.830
In 1995, Kim Jong-un was enrolled in a private college in Bern, under the name Pak-un.

01:05:13.070 --> 01:05:14.750
He was to receive a normal education.

01:05:16.270 --> 01:05:22.130
At the time, Kim Jong-un was very athletic, and spoke quite a bit of French and German,

01:05:22.450 --> 01:05:25.350
He didn't see many people.

01:05:27.950 --> 01:05:32.203
He was surrounded by 2-3 other very young-looking Koreans who pretended to be

01:05:32.203 --> 01:05:34.634
students, when in fact they were bodyguards.

01:05:35.990 --> 01:05:40.410
The kids thought he was the son of a diplomat.

01:05:42.570 --> 01:05:47.230
He was very introverted and loyal to the few friends he had.

01:05:48.810 --> 01:05:53.790
I think he really wanted to have a normal childhood, with normal relationships.

01:05:56.980 --> 01:06:01.600
At the age of 14, Kim Jong-un seems happy to be away from the hassles of the palace,

01:06:02.860 --> 01:06:06.991
because 8,000 kilometers away, his father finds himself embroiled in an

01:06:06.991 --> 01:06:08.271
international scandal.

01:06:09.300 --> 01:06:13.640
The dramatic situation in North Korea, faced with a terrible famine,

01:06:14.140 --> 01:06:18.180
After Médecins du Monde, Médecins Sans Frontières announced its departure from

01:06:18.180 --> 01:06:21.548
the country, demanding greater transparency from the authorities.

01:06:22.060 --> 01:06:26.905
Some talk of 3 million victims in a country where information is very difficult

01:06:26.905 --> 01:06:27.518
to verify.

01:06:28.650 --> 01:06:34.220
In October 1998, several NGOs announced their departure from North Korea.

01:06:35.300 --> 01:06:39.450
They accused the Pyongyang regime of diverting all humanitarian aid intended for

01:06:39.450 --> 01:06:40.228
the population.

01:06:44.880 --> 01:06:48.800
We decided to leave because we judged our own aid to be ineffective,

01:06:49.440 --> 01:06:52.881
from the point of view of the people it was supposed to help. In other words,

01:06:52.881 --> 01:06:56.815
the so-called sick in great distress, the so-called population groups in great distress,

01:06:57.420 --> 01:06:59.100
we didn't really have access to them.

01:07:08.680 --> 01:07:12.722
The resources sent by international organizations should have been distributed

01:07:12.722 --> 01:07:13.448
to the people.

01:07:14.280 --> 01:07:19.800
But in fact, it was the privileged class, the military and the police, who benefited.

01:07:21.190 --> 01:07:26.639
By diverting humanitarian aid, Kim Jong-il was able to maintain his army and,

01:07:26.639 --> 01:07:28.409
consequently, his regime.

01:07:29.160 --> 01:07:32.985
But he did so at the cost of a famine that decimated more than 10% of his

01:07:32.985 --> 01:07:34.347
population in three years.

01:07:37.650 --> 01:07:41.734
The international community believed that the North Korean regime would collapse

01:07:41.734 --> 01:07:43.418
with the fall of the Soviet Union

01:07:43.470 --> 01:07:47.736
and that its nuclear program was under control thanks to the agreements signed

01:07:47.736 --> 01:07:48.775
under Bill Clinton.

01:07:49.010 --> 01:07:52.790
But the attacks in New York on September 11, 2001 changed everything.

01:07:53.170 --> 01:07:57.889
The new American president, George W. Bush, placed North Korea on the axis of

01:07:57.889 --> 01:07:59.728
evil alongside Iran and Syria,

01:07:59.790 --> 01:08:03.890
countries likely to supply terrorists with weapons of mass destruction.

01:08:04.330 --> 01:08:09.220
Above all, the American secret services were to discover that the Pyongyang

01:08:09.220 --> 01:08:10.980
regime was doing just fine,

01:08:11.478 --> 01:08:14.264
thanks to a most unexpected financing system.

01:08:26.110 --> 01:08:30.981
On May 20, 2003, two high-ranking North Korean officials who had fled their

01:08:30.981 --> 01:08:33.515
country testified before the US Senate.

01:08:37.190 --> 01:08:41.338
With their faces masked, they revealed the most unspoken secrets of Kim

01:08:41.338 --> 01:08:42.331
Jong-il's regime.

01:08:44.682 --> 01:08:49.897
We're busy manufacturing and selling legal drugs to other countries to support

01:08:49.897 --> 01:08:52.104
the regime from junkyard to cage.

01:08:52.314 --> 01:08:55.972
to support a financially strangled regime.

01:08:56.009 --> 01:09:01.967
North Korea must be the only regime in the world

01:09:02.017 --> 01:09:06.712
to have set up a state-level drug trafficking business.

01:09:07.810 --> 01:09:13.010
They were high-level defecators. They were clearing up important questions.

01:09:13.730 --> 01:09:19.010
How can a small country like North Korea survive and continue its weapons program?

01:09:21.090 --> 01:09:25.790
They tell of their own role in this organized government crime.

01:09:26.690 --> 01:09:31.030
They explain the collusion between North Korea and foreign mafias.

01:09:32.870 --> 01:09:37.795
U.S. senators are stunned to discover the existence of Bureau 39 and its

01:09:37.795 --> 01:09:40.941
involvement in international drug trafficking.

01:09:45.230 --> 01:09:51.300
Methamphetamines, synthetic drugs, have now replaced the heroin production of

01:09:51.300 --> 01:09:51.931
the 80s.

01:09:53.530 --> 01:09:58.574
Over the past 30 years, North Korean drug and contraband trafficking has taken

01:09:58.574 --> 01:10:00.385
on unimaginable proportions.

01:10:04.380 --> 01:10:08.380
It's worth billions, there's no doubt about it. Billions of dollars.

01:10:08.840 --> 01:10:12.507
We don't talk about millions anymore, because you have to include revenues from

01:10:12.507 --> 01:10:15.153
drugs, contraband, fake cigarettes and counterfeit bills.

01:10:21.770 --> 01:10:30.710
70 to 80% of the currency collected by North Korea is illegitimate and illegal.

01:10:32.050 --> 01:10:37.532
Comparing North Korea to the Italian Mafia is interesting, but it overlooks the

01:10:37.532 --> 01:10:38.920
difference in scale.

01:10:40.190 --> 01:10:46.251
The Italian mafia, even at its peak in the 70s and 80s, never reached the

01:10:46.251 --> 01:10:52.063
sophistication, size and global reach of North Korean organized crime.

01:11:01.350 --> 01:11:05.531
We were becoming aware that their weapons programs were being developed thanks

01:11:05.531 --> 01:11:07.836
to the revenues from this kind of activity.

01:11:18.080 --> 01:11:22.760
American investigations are also uncovering disturbing alliances.

01:11:24.010 --> 01:11:29.428
In February 2004, Abdul Kader Khan, the father of the Pakistani atomic bomb, was

01:11:29.428 --> 01:11:32.002
arrested by the Pakistani authorities.

01:11:34.160 --> 01:11:40.716
He admitted having sold centrifuges to North Korea, the devices used to enrich

01:11:40.716 --> 01:11:42.565
uranium to make bombs.

01:11:45.320 --> 01:11:48.180
Abdul Kader Khan had helped the North Koreans to prepare.

01:11:48.980 --> 01:11:53.178
First, he gave them a starter kit for two dozen centrifuges of two different

01:11:53.178 --> 01:11:54.504
types in the late 1990s.

01:11:55.800 --> 01:11:58.240
Then he taught them how to operate them.

01:11:59.630 --> 01:12:03.442
They then managed to assemble all these parts and started building more

01:12:03.442 --> 01:12:07.416
centrifuges themselves. The North Koreans are very, very good technically.

01:12:09.610 --> 01:12:13.930
The program could be run in a room the size of my apartment.

01:12:14.450 --> 01:12:17.850
The research and development didn't require any special facilities.

01:12:19.780 --> 01:12:25.340
Faced with this damning information, the Bush administration decided to strike a blow.

01:12:28.610 --> 01:12:33.340
If we wanted to stop North Korea's nuclear program, we had to block the money.

01:12:34.180 --> 01:12:39.893
The Treasury realized that North Korea was using an offshore bank to manage its

01:12:39.893 --> 01:12:41.267
illicit activities.

01:12:42.780 --> 01:12:47.326
On September 25, 2005, the US Treasury designated Banco Delta Asia as an

01:12:47.326 --> 01:12:50.736
accomplice in Pyongyang's money-laundering activities.

01:12:52.180 --> 01:12:54.660
All North Korean assets were frozen.

01:12:56.790 --> 01:13:00.726
When sanctions were imposed on the bank, the North Koreans started screaming

01:13:00.726 --> 01:13:01.658
like never before.

01:13:01.710 --> 01:13:05.750
It was clear that we had touched a sensitive point in their system, because

01:13:05.750 --> 01:13:09.036
Banco Delta Asia was the main bank for their money transfers.

01:13:14.250 --> 01:13:18.882
The other banks started thinking "if the US sanctions me, I'm going to be

01:13:18.882 --> 01:13:22.246
associated with North Korea and that's not worth it".

01:13:22.310 --> 01:13:25.650
So we were able to disconnect them from the international banking system.

01:13:27.390 --> 01:13:31.547
But these economic sanctions will not weaken the North Koreans. Quite the

01:13:31.547 --> 01:13:32.573
contrary, in fact.

01:13:36.260 --> 01:13:41.930
On October 9, 2006, a communiqué from Pyongyang took the Americans by storm.

01:13:43.570 --> 01:13:47.570
North Korea had just successfully carried out its first nuclear test.

01:13:49.870 --> 01:13:52.490
It was only a partial success.

01:13:53.310 --> 01:13:56.470
And the explosive power was weak, on the order of a fizzle.

01:13:57.510 --> 01:13:58.850
But it was a shock.

01:14:00.310 --> 01:14:05.488
One of the Bush administration's mistakes with North Korea was to let an

01:14:05.488 --> 01:14:11.243
identified threat, sealed up and under camera surveillance, materialize in a few

01:14:11.243 --> 01:14:14.336
years and become a functional nuclear bomb.

01:14:19.140 --> 01:14:24.320
There are few events that change the way a country is perceived by others.

01:14:25.820 --> 01:14:30.520
With the 2006 nuclear test, North Korea radically changed its status.

01:14:32.440 --> 01:14:36.260
It's a demonstration of power.

01:14:37.620 --> 01:14:41.204
They're showing that they're not going to let themselves be pushed around and

01:14:41.204 --> 01:14:43.113
that they won't back down under pressure.

01:14:50.690 --> 01:14:56.249
There was real concern about the reaction of the United States, because North

01:14:56.249 --> 01:15:00.797
Korea had crossed a real red line with this first nuclear test.

01:15:01.690 --> 01:15:06.250
And President Bush had just invaded Iraq and Afghanistan.

01:15:07.020 --> 01:15:11.280
Indeed, the United States has other priorities.

01:15:13.300 --> 01:15:17.166
Embroiled in several wars in the Middle East, George W. Bush does not want

01:15:17.166 --> 01:15:18.367
another armed conflict.

01:15:19.780 --> 01:15:22.160
He prefers to opt for negotiation.

01:15:24.560 --> 01:15:29.220
Bush had been contemptuous of the North Koreans, and he really hated them.

01:15:32.120 --> 01:15:39.300
But by 2005, he knew he'd made the wrong decisions in Afghanistan and Iraq.

01:15:40.280 --> 01:15:43.600
And I think he also knew what a mistake he'd made with North Korea.

01:15:44.360 --> 01:15:48.160
That's why he reacted to the nuclear tests by advocating a negotiated solution.

01:15:56.980 --> 01:16:01.701
Kim Jong-il has succeeded. He now has nuclear weapons, and the international

01:16:01.701 --> 01:16:03.937
community is very worried about him.

01:16:04.160 --> 01:16:08.620
Attacking him would mean risking a retaliation and a terrible escalation for everyone.

01:16:09.120 --> 01:16:13.622
But at 66, the dictator is not at his best. At the end of the 2000s, the

01:16:13.622 --> 01:16:16.937
question of the regime's continuity once again arose.

01:16:19.260 --> 01:16:24.130
Kim Jong-il was about to designate the person who would take over the dynasty.

01:16:25.280 --> 01:16:29.560
Having survived a stroke in 2008, he didn't want to take any risks.

01:16:31.160 --> 01:16:35.200
Kim Jong-il suffered from numerous health problems.

01:16:36.380 --> 01:16:40.540
Heart, kidney, liver. He had high blood pressure and was overweight.

01:16:43.870 --> 01:16:48.440
Like his father before him, he sought his successor among his children.

01:16:50.050 --> 01:16:54.190
Logically, he could have chosen his eldest son, Kim Jong-nam.

01:16:54.970 --> 01:16:56.910
But he has too bad a reputation.

01:16:58.030 --> 01:17:02.126
He spends more time in China than in North Korea and doesn't seem to have the

01:17:02.126 --> 01:17:03.136
soul of a dictator.

01:17:03.470 --> 01:17:06.930
It doesn't fit because the character doesn't fit.

01:17:07.370 --> 01:17:09.450
Kim Jong-nam doesn't like the army, it bores him.

01:17:09.830 --> 01:17:13.126
For a militaristic regime, that's something that doesn't fit. He's too curious,

01:17:13.126 --> 01:17:14.128
he travels abroad a lot.

01:17:14.550 --> 01:17:16.910
He went to Shanghai, for example, and came back enthusiastic.

01:17:19.260 --> 01:17:22.640
When Kim Jong-nam was still at the heart of the regime,

01:17:22.960 --> 01:17:26.060
he was in favor of Chinese-style economic reforms.

01:17:26.640 --> 01:17:28.140
And his father didn't like that.

01:17:29.500 --> 01:17:34.000
And gradually, we see a break between father and son, albeit in fits and starts.

01:17:35.060 --> 01:17:39.848
Kim Jong-il therefore chose another successor, his youngest son, Kim Jong-un,

01:17:39.848 --> 01:17:42.397
who completed his studies in Switzerland.

01:17:57.690 --> 01:18:02.340
On October 10, 2010, during the party's 65th anniversary,

01:18:03.040 --> 01:18:07.040
Kim Jong-un made his first official appearance alongside his father.

01:18:09.260 --> 01:18:12.380
He has just completed military training and possesses an undeniable asset,

01:18:13.220 --> 01:18:17.180
he bears a striking resemblance to his founding father, Kim Il-sung.

01:18:18.478 --> 01:18:20.970
Kim Jong-un is the spitting image of his grandfather.

01:18:21.350 --> 01:18:24.750
He's tall like him, massive like him, and he loves the army.

01:18:25.070 --> 01:18:28.792
He's in the army all the time, wearing a fur coat, he loves to work out, he does

01:18:28.792 --> 01:18:32.701
exercises with soldiers. He's extraordinarily popular, a true military man at heart.

01:18:33.520 --> 01:18:37.040
Kim Jong-un is the spitting image of his grandfather.

01:18:38.540 --> 01:18:43.000
He's strong-willed, determined and has a big ego.

01:18:43.700 --> 01:18:47.940
It's like in the Hollywood film The Godfather.

01:18:50.400 --> 01:18:51.880
Marlon Brando has 3 sons.

01:18:52.860 --> 01:18:58.740
The first is a heavy drinker and a womanizer. The second is a little weak.

01:19:00.550 --> 01:19:03.090
And the third is exactly like his father.

01:19:07.060 --> 01:19:12.080
From that day on, Kim Jong-un's rise was to be meteoric.

01:19:24.700 --> 01:19:27.680
No one had foreseen Kim Jong-un's appearance.

01:19:30.220 --> 01:19:33.440
That's why the world's media and experts were surprised.

01:19:38.940 --> 01:19:42.700
He was the son of Kim Jong-il's mistress.

01:19:43.800 --> 01:19:45.720
I thought it was really disgusting.

01:19:46.760 --> 01:19:47.760
It didn't make sense.

01:19:50.500 --> 01:19:56.460
How could a country with such a hereditary system exist? I was shocked.

01:19:59.280 --> 01:20:04.075
For the succession to take place smoothly, the regime is going to display all

01:20:04.075 --> 01:20:04.697
its power.

01:20:05.810 --> 01:20:08.540
In particular, its nuclear power.

01:20:16.630 --> 01:20:17.970
One month after this ceremony,

01:20:19.350 --> 01:20:24.250
two of the world's leading nuclear specialists were invited to North Korea.

01:20:25.340 --> 01:20:27.480
The first is Siegfried Hecker,

01:20:28.160 --> 01:20:31.820
former director of an American nuclear weapons research laboratory.

01:20:34.320 --> 01:20:37.500
The second is Robert Carlin.

01:20:38.470 --> 01:20:43.130
He is a former CIA agent. These two independent experts will visit Yongbyon,

01:20:43.730 --> 01:20:48.210
North Korea's most secret nuclear site.

01:20:51.360 --> 01:20:52.920
They led us into a large building.

01:20:53.420 --> 01:20:55.320
In a control room,

01:20:56.220 --> 01:20:59.080
there were several technicians in white with computers.

01:21:00.120 --> 01:21:04.220
They took us to a window, and there we were speechless.

01:21:09.590 --> 01:21:12.090
My mouth must have been hanging open.

01:21:12.090 --> 01:21:14.050
I couldn't believe my eyes.

01:21:20.010 --> 01:21:24.490
In front of us were around 2,000 centrifuges, by a rough estimate.

01:21:25.750 --> 01:21:27.410
It was a brand-new installation.

01:21:29.800 --> 01:21:31.160
They wanted us to see it.

01:21:31.620 --> 01:21:34.500
That was the purpose of our visit. They wanted the Americans to know.

01:21:36.290 --> 01:21:38.150
The two men are clearly stunned.

01:21:39.560 --> 01:21:41.240
The sight of these centrifuges,

01:21:41.820 --> 01:21:47.060
opens up terrifying perspectives on North Korea's nuclear capabilities.

01:21:49.060 --> 01:21:51.140
How many centrifuges do they have?

01:21:51.760 --> 01:21:57.760
How much uranium can they really manufacture? And the answer is "we don't know".

01:22:01.280 --> 01:22:03.520
By my reckoning,

01:22:04.280 --> 01:22:08.930
they have enough plutonium and enriched uranium to make 20 to 25 bombs.

01:22:09.840 --> 01:22:11.930
And they have the capacity to make a bomb,

01:22:12.560 --> 01:22:13.920
every 6 to 7 weeks.

01:22:16.720 --> 01:22:17.860
A new atomic bomb,

01:22:18.640 --> 01:22:19.960
every 6 weeks.

01:22:27.400 --> 01:22:31.500
The conclusion is that international sanctions have had no effect.

01:22:42.800 --> 01:22:51.360
The building housing the centrifuges had been under constant surveillance for years.

01:22:52.120 --> 01:22:55.260
And no intelligence service, as far as I know,

01:22:55.820 --> 01:23:02.454
saw a single centrifuge arrive in that building. Does this mean that our

01:23:02.454 --> 01:23:05.587
intelligence services are no good?

01:23:05.680 --> 01:23:09.000
No, it just means that you can't track a centrifuge.

01:23:09.560 --> 01:23:11.815
It's just too easy to hide.

01:23:12.321 --> 01:23:16.443
As for the political message, it's unambiguous.

01:23:16.691 --> 01:23:19.385
Kim Jong-un, the third in line,

01:23:19.480 --> 01:23:23.760
will not stop the nuclear program initiated by his father and grandfather.

01:23:30.830 --> 01:23:34.926
The North Koreans wanted to be ready to be in a position of strength when the

01:23:34.926 --> 01:23:35.936
heir came to power.

01:23:37.790 --> 01:23:42.415
They needed to be as strong as possible during this period when the outside

01:23:42.415 --> 01:23:45.128
world perceived them as weak and vulnerable.

01:24:01.450 --> 01:24:05.770
Kim Jong-il died of a heart attack in December 2011.

01:24:06.842 --> 01:24:08.070
History repeats itself.

01:24:08.890 --> 01:24:12.930
As soon as the funeral took place, his successor, Kim Jong-un, took center stage.

01:24:14.400 --> 01:24:17.020
He accompanied the body of the deceased dictator,

01:24:17.210 --> 01:24:20.910
before a crowd in collective hysteria.

01:24:27.100 --> 01:24:31.320
The young Kim Jong-un is seen walking bareheaded,

01:24:31.540 --> 01:24:33.900
braving the cold in front of the catafalque.

01:24:34.890 --> 01:24:37.970
We see the entire Korean people braving the cold.

01:24:38.390 --> 01:24:40.970
From the moment the heir, young Kim Jong-un,

01:24:41.410 --> 01:24:44.350
walked alone in front of the coffin, bareheaded,

01:24:44.690 --> 01:24:46.490
the people had to do the same.

01:24:47.700 --> 01:24:52.320
That day, a handful of men accompanied the heir around the funeral vehicle.

01:24:54.130 --> 01:24:59.292
This was the regency team set up by Kim Jong-il to supervise his son during his

01:24:59.292 --> 01:25:00.664
first years in power.

01:25:06.680 --> 01:25:08.040
Unlike his father,

01:25:08.480 --> 01:25:11.540
who had been in the party apparatus since 1964,

01:25:12.060 --> 01:25:13.780
30 years before inheriting power,

01:25:14.700 --> 01:25:18.575
Kim Jong-un had very little time to learn how to manipulate the various echelons

01:25:18.575 --> 01:25:19.011
of power.

01:25:20.660 --> 01:25:24.840
Kim Jong-il therefore created a kind of network around himself to ensure his

01:25:24.840 --> 01:25:25.665
son's survival.

01:25:27.324 --> 01:25:30.490
Behind the heir, the man in the black coat,

01:25:31.230 --> 01:25:33.161
is General Jang Song-taek.

01:25:33.290 --> 01:25:36.270
It's his uncle, one of the regime's most powerful men.

01:25:36.810 --> 01:25:42.884
He was supposed to bring all his knowledge of defense and military matters to

01:25:42.884 --> 01:25:43.831
Kim Jong-un.

01:25:48.210 --> 01:25:53.130
Jang Song-thaek is the regent who oversees the economy and relations with China.

01:25:54.450 --> 01:25:57.930
He also explains policy to Kim Jong-un.

01:26:00.262 --> 01:26:06.314
The question on everyone's lips is, what will be the attitude of this new North

01:26:06.314 --> 01:26:07.463
Korean monarch?

01:26:09.970 --> 01:26:13.832
Kim Jong-un's Swiss education raised a lot of hopes in the United States and the

01:26:13.832 --> 01:26:14.701
rest of the world.

01:26:15.630 --> 01:26:18.770
Many thought it would make him more open to reform.

01:26:19.260 --> 01:26:22.820
We didn't know anything about him, but since he had lived abroad,

01:26:23.020 --> 01:26:25.640
maybe he would change his business model.

01:26:26.292 --> 01:26:30.267
And from his very first public appearances, Kim Jong-un has been sending out

01:26:30.267 --> 01:26:31.104
signs of change,

01:26:31.240 --> 01:26:33.360
like the presence of his wife by his side.

01:26:39.420 --> 01:26:42.955
We said, "There, just like elsewhere, just like in the West, just like in the

01:26:42.955 --> 01:26:44.654
United States, there's a first lady."

01:26:45.480 --> 01:26:50.180
That day, the couple came to see a show inspired by Walt Disney characters,

01:26:51.100 --> 01:26:54.140
an American symbol previously banned in Pyongyang.

01:27:05.790 --> 01:27:11.310
It's a bit childish, it's not very sophisticated, Minnie, Donald, etc., dancing.

01:27:11.610 --> 01:27:21.410
Still, it's quite a step for a regime that has tended to make Manichean accusations

01:27:22.050 --> 01:27:25.550
in relation to this American junk culture.

01:27:29.780 --> 01:27:33.580
He tried to send a message.

01:27:34.940 --> 01:27:38.740
If you recognize me as the leader of a nuclear power,

01:27:39.660 --> 01:27:41.980
then I'm ready to make concessions.

01:27:44.280 --> 01:27:48.860
If you guarantee the survival and security of my regime,

01:27:51.060 --> 01:27:53.920
I won't behave like my father.

01:27:57.830 --> 01:28:03.210
But beneath his harmless exterior, Kim Jong-un hides another face,

01:28:04.210 --> 01:28:08.250
that of a dictator even more violent and radical than his predecessors.

01:28:13.830 --> 01:28:16.930
On December 8th, 2013, in the middle of a party meeting,

01:28:17.810 --> 01:28:22.937
to everyone's surprise, Kim Jong-un ordered the immediate arrest of his uncle,

01:28:22.937 --> 01:28:26.684
Jang Song-thaek, the mentor chosen for him by his father.

01:28:28.170 --> 01:28:31.750
Jang controlled the money from foreign trade.

01:28:33.470 --> 01:28:37.430
And when Kim Jong-un needed these funds, he had to go through him.

01:28:39.850 --> 01:28:43.830
Kim Jong-un didn't have absolute power, and that enraged him.

01:28:47.800 --> 01:28:50.320
To oust this uncle, who had taken on too much power,

01:28:50.860 --> 01:28:55.620
Kim Jong-un accused him of treason, corruption and promiscuity.

01:28:56.260 --> 01:28:59.280
A public humiliation that doesn't stop there.

01:29:04.583 --> 01:29:07.590
Having someone of Jang Song-taek's stature,

01:29:08.680 --> 01:29:12.050
walk out of a political bureau meeting in front of the entire leadership team,

01:29:13.020 --> 01:29:14.020
and in front of the whole world,

01:29:15.800 --> 01:29:20.636
and then exhibited at the trial, with bruises on his face, sends a very strong

01:29:20.636 --> 01:29:22.558
message to the regime's cadres.

01:29:25.320 --> 01:29:30.040
The message is that there is only one leader, and that leader is Kim Jong-un.

01:29:33.310 --> 01:29:37.860
After a summary trial, Jang Song-taek was executed.

01:29:39.130 --> 01:29:43.130
Such violence shocked everyone, including those in North Korea.

01:29:45.310 --> 01:29:50.890
I couldn't imagine Kim killing his uncle like that.

01:29:52.500 --> 01:29:53.780
It was shocking.

01:29:56.470 --> 01:30:01.670
Because in North Korea, members of the Kim family didn't kill each other.

01:30:04.130 --> 01:30:06.630
Of course, there have always been executions of high-ranking officials,

01:30:07.610 --> 01:30:09.130
but that was behind the curtain.

01:30:10.770 --> 01:30:13.750
Never like this, in public.

01:30:20.354 --> 01:30:23.060
We knew this was just the beginning,

01:30:24.880 --> 01:30:27.600
that even more frightening events were to come.

01:30:29.250 --> 01:30:34.107
In the months that followed, Kim Jong-un ruthlessly eliminated all high-ranking

01:30:34.107 --> 01:30:37.858
Korean dignitaries and party cadres likely to overshadow him.

01:30:39.940 --> 01:30:44.580
An unprecedented purge that began to worry his powerful neighbor China.

01:30:49.910 --> 01:30:53.990
Until then, China had always supported the Kim regime.

01:30:55.180 --> 01:31:00.020
North Korea serves as a bulwark against the American presence in South Korea.

01:31:01.190 --> 01:31:04.130
But Kim Jong-un is proving to be uncontrollable,

01:31:04.870 --> 01:31:07.330
Beijing reportedly considered removing him from power.

01:31:10.430 --> 01:31:15.390
China was in favor of regime change in North Korea.

01:31:18.830 --> 01:31:22.570
A surgical operation to replace Kim Jong-un,

01:31:23.210 --> 01:31:26.630
which would suit both the United States and South Korea.

01:31:29.260 --> 01:31:34.500
One of the potential replacements could be Kim Jong-nam, his elder brother.

01:31:35.170 --> 01:31:37.690
The one their father did not want as successor.

01:31:38.890 --> 01:31:41.610
He has been living under Chinese protection for several years.

01:31:43.310 --> 01:31:48.910
That day, he was at Kuala Lumpur airport, returning from a trip to Malaysia.

01:31:54.130 --> 01:31:59.315
A year earlier, political refugees in exile had asked Kim Jong-nam to become the

01:31:59.315 --> 01:32:01.325
head of a dissident government.

01:32:02.610 --> 01:32:03.270
He refused.

01:32:06.010 --> 01:32:10.150
The North Korean government immediately ordered him to return.

01:32:11.710 --> 01:32:13.950
Once again, Kim Jong-nam refused.

01:32:16.590 --> 01:32:22.050
Kim Jong-nam has the ideal profile, both close to Beijing and a member of the

01:32:22.050 --> 01:32:23.539
North Korean dynasty.

01:32:24.330 --> 01:32:28.290
His appointment would allow China to take control without destabilizing the regime.

01:32:30.070 --> 01:32:33.170
But he will never return from his trip to Malaysia.

01:32:33.170 --> 01:32:43.470
We see Kim Jong-nam, a businessman, walking quietly, unescorted, without a bodyguard,

01:32:46.920 --> 01:32:53.720
only to be abruptly joined by two women who place their hands on his face before disappearing.

01:32:59.350 --> 01:33:04.110
The scene, filmed by airport cameras, lasted just a few seconds.

01:33:05.260 --> 01:33:09.560
After spraying him in the face with liquid, the 2 women melt into the crowd.

01:33:11.450 --> 01:33:14.970
Kim Jong-nam, taken aback, did not react.

01:33:16.110 --> 01:33:20.970
But a few minutes later, he collapsed and fainted.

01:33:23.370 --> 01:33:29.818
It was soon learned that he had been out of breath and had gone to the clinic,

01:33:29.818 --> 01:33:32.547
where he died shortly afterwards.

01:33:33.050 --> 01:33:38.550
So the assassination was staged in spectacular fashion, and it's all very mysterious.

01:33:40.600 --> 01:33:47.858
The sophistication of the operation, the acquisition of equipment, the modus

01:33:47.858 --> 01:33:55.212
operandi and the extent of the network required are all clues pointing to the

01:33:55.212 --> 01:33:57.408
involvement of a state.

01:33:59.330 --> 01:34:06.070
Malaysian authorities found traces of a powerful nerve agent on the victim's face.

01:34:07.250 --> 01:34:10.890
The North Koreans deny any involvement in the assassination.

01:34:11.550 --> 01:34:15.330
But the method used makes them the main suspects.

01:34:16.290 --> 01:34:20.862
The North Korean government has a very long history of very, very daring

01:34:20.862 --> 01:34:22.386
intelligence operations.

01:34:23.470 --> 01:34:26.510
They have commandos specialized in targeted assassinations.

01:34:27.290 --> 01:34:29.930
They are among the best in the world.

01:34:33.252 --> 01:34:39.502
The message behind this assassination is guys, you're going to have to deal with

01:34:39.502 --> 01:34:41.221
me one way or another.

01:34:42.680 --> 01:34:47.661
In just a few years, Kim Jong-un has eliminated all those who could threaten his

01:34:47.661 --> 01:34:49.217
power within the country.

01:34:53.130 --> 01:34:57.588
And to earn the respect of the international community, he's banking on his

01:34:57.588 --> 01:34:58.420
nuclear power.

01:34:59.100 --> 01:35:00.500
He's going to make a spectacle of it.

01:35:02.770 --> 01:35:08.150
Every missile launch, every atomic bomb test will be staged to arouse fear.

01:35:12.790 --> 01:35:16.770
Under Kim Jong-un, there is a tendency to harden positions.

01:35:18.730 --> 01:35:22.270
Permanent demonstrations of force that get more extreme every time.

01:35:25.310 --> 01:35:27.510
He's spiraling further and further out of control.

01:35:37.580 --> 01:35:43.363
The number of tests, both ballistic and nuclear, under the young leader's reign

01:35:43.363 --> 01:35:45.046
has doubled or tripled.

01:35:52.250 --> 01:35:57.256
Nuclear and missile tests are also there to show that the regime will survive,

01:35:57.256 --> 01:36:00.465
and that it's in everyone's interest to accept it.

01:36:07.570 --> 01:36:11.951
We're at a critical juncture where nothing seems to stop the North Koreans'

01:36:11.951 --> 01:36:14.931
determination to develop the capacity to strike us.

01:36:17.010 --> 01:36:20.010
This presents the United States with some very difficult choices.

01:36:22.410 --> 01:36:27.170
In July 2017, Kim Jong-un witnessed the launch of a new intercontinental missile.

01:36:46.910 --> 01:36:52.380
The young dictator had just fulfilled his grandfather's dream of putting the

01:36:52.380 --> 01:36:54.828
United States within firing range.

01:36:55.640 --> 01:36:59.140
A reasonable projection is estimated at around 10,000 kilometers.

01:36:59.140 --> 01:37:04.401
In other words, part of the US territory is already accessible, the West Coast

01:37:04.401 --> 01:37:06.492
and perhaps the East Coast too.

01:37:10.930 --> 01:37:14.956
It remains to be seen whether North Korea has already achieved, or is about to

01:37:14.956 --> 01:37:16.918
achieve, the Grail, the ultimate goal,

01:37:17.050 --> 01:37:22.075
i.e. to place an operational nuclear weapon on a ballistic missile that can have

01:37:22.075 --> 01:37:25.467
an intercontinental range, reaching as far as the USA.

01:37:26.230 --> 01:37:29.725
Have they already achieved this goal? It's not certain, but what is certain is

01:37:29.725 --> 01:37:30.845
that they're not far off.

01:37:32.300 --> 01:37:36.340
The United States is now within theoretical range of North Korean missiles.

01:37:38.200 --> 01:37:42.340
A situation that has the new American president, Donald Trump, in a tizzy.

01:37:43.850 --> 01:37:47.580
He reacts violently to every provocation from Kim Jong-un.

01:37:51.089 --> 01:37:57.652
North Korea had better stop threatening the United States,

01:37:57.760 --> 01:38:05.223
or it will face fire and fury on a scale the world has never seen before.

01:38:06.200 --> 01:38:11.243
There's only one person in the world today who's more unpredictable than Kim

01:38:11.243 --> 01:38:13.433
Jong-un, and that's Donald Trump.

01:38:14.300 --> 01:38:16.460
There's no way of predicting what might happen.

01:38:24.770 --> 01:38:29.076
The risk of an uncontrolled escalation or a poorly managed incident is even

01:38:29.076 --> 01:38:33.555
greater today between North Korea and the United States than it was during the

01:38:33.555 --> 01:38:35.795
Cold War between Moscow and Washington.

01:38:41.080 --> 01:38:43.900
North Korea specialists are at their wits' end.

01:38:46.430 --> 01:38:51.590
The situation has deteriorated to such an extent that disaster seems inevitable.

01:38:52.670 --> 01:38:57.363
We no longer know what to do with North Korea. Everything has been tried.

01:39:00.557 --> 01:39:02.850
The moment of truth is approaching.

01:39:07.810 --> 01:39:12.010
A conventional war would be devastating. But if there is a nuclear escalation,

01:39:12.010 --> 01:39:14.056
the consequences will be unimaginable.

